---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About — notesdaq">
  <div class="about">
    <h1>How notesdaq works</h1>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      <h2>The concept</h2>
      <p>
        Every reblog on Tumblr is retroactively treated as a stock purchase. When you reblog a post, your "buy price"
        is the number of reblogs that post had at that moment. As the post continues to spread, your investment grows.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you reblogged a post when it had 10 reblogs and it now has 1,000, your multiplier is 100x.
        If you were the original poster, your buy price is 0 &mdash; infinite return.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      <h2>Scoring</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Share price</strong> = total number of reblogs on the root post</li>
        <li><strong>Buy price</strong> = the share price at the moment of your reblog</li>
        <li><strong>Multiplier</strong> = current price / buy price</li>
        <li><strong>Portfolio value</strong> = sum of current prices across all your positions</li>
        <li>OP gets a synthetic position at price 0 (displayed as +Inf multiplier)</li>
        <li>Multiple reblogs of the same post = multiple positions</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      <h2>Data source</h2>
      <p>
        notesdaq uses the public Tumblr API v2 to enumerate every reblog on tracked posts. Share prices are
        derived by sorting all reblogs chronologically and assigning sequential counts. No real money is involved,
        no accounts are needed, and no opt-in is required &mdash; all data is from public posts.
      </p>
      <p>
        The crawl is ongoing. Only blogs that have been crawled will show portfolio data. If your blog isn't here yet,
        it may be in the queue &mdash; check back later.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Why?</h2>
      <p>Because it's fun. And because every time you reblog a post at 3 notes that later goes to 50,000, you deserve credit for your impeccable taste.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .about h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .about h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .about p {
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .about ul {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
